+## Runtime statistics
+
+### Play-time checkpoints rewrite history and timed-out synchronization keeps coordinating
+
+- **Symptom:** each play-time checkpoint rewrites a growing JSON history, or a timed-out publication still waits for local file access.
+- **Cause:** atomic JSON replacement rewrites the whole document. A semaphore timeout stops its caller waiting but does not cancel coordinated work.
+- **Fix:** `dm/apple/GameTime` stores local segments in SQLite transactions, updating only increased values and summary metadata. It preserves segment IDs when importing old local JSON and merging the cloud JSON snapshot. `DMGameTimeSyncProgress` cancels both coordinators, with checks before transactions, publication and conflict cleanup. Entered transactions finish or roll back. Runtime flush timeout cancels its own attempts, and iOS background expiration cancels pending publication until resume. No live database is synchronized through the cloud folder.
+- **Found on:** synthetic native timing, restore/clone, concurrent-process, crash-recovery and blocked-coordination tests in `dm/host/tests/t_game_time*.m`. No game-specific timing or physical iCloud transfer is claimed.
